<title>USA: Perceptron Inc Q4 net falls, sales rise.</title>
<headline>Perceptron Inc Q4 net falls, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>PLYMOUTH, Mich. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in $000's except per share data)</p>
<p>		  Fourth Quarter			 Year</p>
<p>	     1996    1995 % Change	 1996     1995 % Change</p>
<p> Net Sales	 16,098  13,388   20%   49,679  37,291    33%</p>
<p> Gross profit    10,197   8,437   21%   30,690  23,116    33%</p>
<p>Non-cash stock compensation expense</p>
<p>			    0	 0    --    3,202   1,377     --</p>
<p> Pre-tax income   5,474   4,141   32%   10,964   7,927    38%</p>
<p> Income tax	 1,583	 0    --    3,070   (482)     --</p>
<p> Net income	 3,891   4,141  (6)%    7,894   8,409   (6)%</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>   per share(A)     .50  .56(A) (10)%     1.03  1.16(A) (11)%</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>			7,706   7,391    4%    7,636   7,258     5%</p>
<p>(A) Net income per share would have been $0.40 and $0.84 for the three and twelve month periods of 1995, respectively, had income been taxed at 1996 rates.</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 year net includes non-cash charge of $2.1 million or $0.27 a share to reflect adjustments in accounting for stock options.</p>
<p>1995 year net includes non-cash charge of $900,000 or $0.12 a share to reflect adjustments in accounting for stock options.</p>
<p>	    ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
